summary:
  "80" stops being the eighties; only "80s" and its spellings are.

history:
  The listener's own example was "rock 80 uk". The suffix is optional on
  purpose, and the fragment asked of the directory is the bare number: its
  tag filter is a substring match, so "80" reaches "80s", "80's", "1980s"
  and "80er" in one question.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      var m = w.match(/^(?:19)?([5-9])0(?:s|'s|er|ies)?$/);

replace:
      var m = w.match(/^(?:19)?([5-9])0(?:s|'s|er|ies)$/);

expect:
  Killed by tst_searchlogic::test_a_decade_is_one_tag_however_it_is_spelled.
  Line-neutral.
